1 NOTE SOURCE CITATION:
2 CONT    Page: page 1-4
2 CONT    Citation Comments: Nugent:  Also as a headright, JAMES HARDAWAY
2 CONT    brother ofJohn, appears for the
2 CONT    first time in the Charles City county records on 25 November
2 CONT    1654, Patent Book No. 3, page 313, when John Drayton entered a
2 CONT patent for 2000 acres of land in  Westmoreland County, Virginia on the
2 CONT southside of Petomeck River. page 301.
2 CONT    Fleet:  A check of records with regard to the 250 acres of land
2 CONT       situated on Kemishes Creek which James Hardaway inherited and
2 CONT       then assigned to his son John Hardaway, reveals an interesting and
2 CONT       important family connection.
2 CONT    Title: Descendants of James Hardaway, Charles City County,
2 CONT Virginia,1650-1800
2 CONT    Author: James F. Devenport, Judith Hardaway Devenport, Laurence
2 CONT B. Gardiner
2 CONT    Publication Information: James F. Devenport, One Winchester
2 CONT Court, Midland,Texas 79705, 1992.
2 CONT SOURCE CITATION:
2 CONT    Page: page 2-6
2 CONT    Text:  Fleet:  A check of records with regard to the 250 acrres
2 CONT    of land situated  on Kemishes Creek which James Hardaway inherited and
2 CONT    thenassigned to his son Joohn Hardaway, reveals an interesting and
2 CONT    important family connection with the Stith Family.  The Stith
2 CONT    Family  plays a substantial role in the Hardaway genealogy for several
2 CONT    generations, as later will be established.
2 CONT    In the Court Records dated 11 June 1661 there is memorandum that
2 CONT    James  Hardaway, for reason of excessive sickness and lameness, was
2 CONT    thereby exempted from all future personal service and taxes
2 CONT    except parish dues (p 243).
2 CONT       By Indenture dated 7 June 1662, James Hardaway of Kemishes Creek in
2 CONT       Charles City County made over to John Stith all his property,
2 CONT       both real and personal, for which John Stith pledged to keep James
2 CONT       Hardaway in good condition for the balance of his life (Fleet,p 271)
2 CONT       Clearly by 1664 however, James Hardaway was still in the world of
2 CONT       the living and was at odds with  John Stith over the 250 acres
2 CONT       on  Kemishes Creek.   You  recall James Hardaway in June 1662 had by
2 CONT       Indenture made over his real and personal property to John Stith.
2 CONT       Then by Septemberr 1664 he had conveyed to his son, JohnHardaway,
2 CONT       the 250 acrees on Kemishes Creek.  Ownership of the land apparently
2 CONT       was the cause of the trouble between James Hardaway and John Stith
2 CONT       as there are several instruments filed of record between James
2 CONT       Hardaway, complainant and John Stith, defendant, in which Stith
2 CONT       DISCLAIMS ALL RIGHTS AND TITLE TO HARDEWAY'S LAND AT KEMISHES
2 CONT       (Fleet p 308) followed by assignment of A PATENT FOR 250 ACRES OF             LAND AT
2 CONT       KEMISHES CREEKE TO  JOHN HARDAWAY, Dated 29 September 1666,
2 CONT       mentions the tract of land was granted to John Stith; was returned
2 CONT       to James Hardaway by assignment; and acquired by Edmund Cowleswith
2 CONT       bill of sale from Jno. Hardaway, dated 3 June 1664 (Childs p 509)
2 CONT    Title: Descendants of James Hardaway, Charles City County, Virginia,
2 CONT    1650-1800.
2 CONT    Author: James F. Devenport, Judith Hardaway Devenport, Laurence
2 CONT    B. Gardiner.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT    Publication Information: James F. Devenport, One Winchester
2 CONT Court, Midland,
2 CONT Texas 79705, 1992
2 CONT    Repository Name: Martha Hewett
2 CONT    Address: 4040 East Greenway Circle, Mesa,
2 CONT             AZ, 85205
