1 NOTE SOURCE CITATION:
2 CONT    Page: p 20
2 CONT    Title: Descendants of James Hardaway, Charles City County,
2 CONT Virginia,
2 CONT 1650-1800
2 CONT    Author: James F. Devenport, Judith Hardaway Devenport, Laurence
2 CONT B. Gardiner
2 CONT    Publication Information: James F. Devenport, One Winchester
2 CONT Court, Midland,
2 CONT Texas 79705, 1992
2 CONT    Repository Name: Martha Hewett
2 CONT    Address: 4040 East Greenway Circle, Mesa,
2 CONT             AZ, 85205
2 CONT    Phone: (602) 807-0750
2 CONT I will write a short history of my life up to the present time.  I
2 CONT was born 26 June 1761 AD on Hatch's Run in Dinwiddie County,
2 CONT Virginia.  There were a good many red skins on Hatch's Run but when
2 CONT the War was over all but the most friendly with the pale fces left.
2 CONT We had no school houses but I tried to get a little learning.  I got
2 CONT so I could read and write and figure a little.  I did not work much,
2 CONT fishing and hunting.  My father's name was Henry Hatch.  He died in
2 CONT 1776.  Then we children had to shift for ourselves.  In 1786, Cozen
2 CONT Billy Beard and I came to North Carolina, Orange County, and I bound
2 CONT myself to Fre McDonnel for seven years at the carpenters trade.  So
2 CONT when I served my time out, I built the first school house in Chappel
2 CONT Hill, NC in 1794 and I got married to Sally Brewer {Cynthia Brewer
2 CONT 13 Nov 1802}.  Then I got a good start.  I had three children by my
2 CONT wife.  We reared four children, one niece whom I adopted.  Her name
2 CONT was Sally Beard. I did not live but six miles from Cozen Billy
2 CONT Beard, and he would come to my house to hunt with me, but my
2 CONT children did not like him.  They said he was so ugly and his hair so
2 CONT long.  They were afraid of him, but I told them he was my first
2 CONT cozen and he was half Indian and that I was close kin to the red
2 CONT man.  I told them that my grandfather Powhatan Beard was a full
2 CONT blood Indian and my mother Sally Beard was half Indian and I was one
2 CONT third Indian.  My grandfather's name was Henry and my father's name
2 CONT was Henry Hatch.
